<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · mountain</p><h1 class="enc-title">Erzberg</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Styrian Erzberg</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Erzberg is a mountain near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eisenerz">Eisenerz</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/styria">Styria</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a>, made largely of siderite iron ore and mined since at least the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a>. Open-cast mining has cut it into giant terraces, giving it the look of a stepped pyramid. Its iron made Styria one of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>'s main iron-producing regions, and it is still worked today.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/erzberg.jpg" alt="Erzberg" width="320" height="220" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Herzi Pinki · CC BY 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:HochtorOedsteinGroup_FromS_HoherZinken.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
